{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/5262-slasher-sentinels-of-gotham","id":5262,"title":"Slasher: Sentinels of Gotham","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-07T11:33:03-08:00","id":5262,"title":"Slasher: Sentinels of Gotham","content":"<b><u>Slasher: Sentinels of Gotham</u></b><br /> <br /> <i>To some, the war for Gotham's soul was won with the defeat of the Joker. Dent's martyrdom was not in vain, they said. It's all a lie. The Joker was not defeated. Dent was no martyr. The truth is out there, yet only few know of it.<br /> <br /> It must remain this way. This is why those in the know are rounded up and offered a choice: Fight for Gotham, or perish in the gutters. The Batman broke his one rule to establish the lie that will be Gothams salvation. We must break it time and again to maintain that lie. Putting our teeth to the curb we will swallow whole the decadence and decay of the city, damning ourselves without hesitation.<br /> <br /> One day The Batman will return and put a final end to the corruption. We must pave the way in blood and fire for that to happen. Come heaven or hell, we will make this the city Batman deserves.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Let's put a bullet in that face</b><br /> Harvey &quot;The White Knight&quot; Dent is dead. The Batman has vanished. The financial backbone of Gotham are either imprisoned for corrupt affairs or disillusioned entirely with life among its inhabitants and have withdrawn from society. The city is poised for regeneration, the so-called &quot;Dent Act&quot; getting close to implementation, but it does so from the lowest of points and with the weakest of willpower. The people are shaken to the core, and the shock from The Joker's assault on their very spirit still hasn't worn off. Theft, fraud and violence is at an all-time high, and with no Dark Knight to fight it, the city is lost.<br /> <br /> That's why the Sentinels exist. They are not your average Batman impersonators, but rather hardened killers carrying on The Batmans work in spirit and symbology but with drastically different methods. They are cunning investigators plucked from their offices to work the streets by cover of cowl and darkness. They are promising scientists offered funding they never dreamed of in return for clandestine services. Engineers, doctors and brawlers, these people are monitored for their potential and then finally recruited with a merciless ultimatum: Join us or die. Noone must know the truth about the Sentinels, because the Sentinels know truths about Gotham, Batman and the &quot;Dent Act&quot; that noone should. Brainwashed and forced to love the kill, the Sentinels do the dark deeds that keep Gotham running until the return of The Batman.<br /> <br /> <b>From the shadows they come</b><br /> Such a tightly organized operation requires funding. Few Sentinels know where their equipment and training comes from, and most don't care to ask. Those who do, know only that their patron, and pressumably founder, is an enigmatic individual that communicates only from the shadows and with technological voice distortion from untracable sources. It identifies itself as &quot;The Fox&quot;. Accepting the nocturnal moniker for their provider, the inner circle of the Sentinels keep the others in line. Cells of Sentinels work independently in their assigned districts, but any cell can be given an order from a superior cell at any time, an order they must follow lest they be punished. For the most part, the Sentinels do crime-fighting. The lethal kind. They wear black, anonymous outfits for most of their operations, but seldom do they clothe themselves in bat-like trappings, preferring complete anonymity. When they do dress in bat imagery, it is often to frame the poor misguided Batman impersonators for their own misdeeds. If you find yourself blocking the way of progress towards peace and justice, you will soon find yourself trapped in your own burning penthouse, or hanging by your stolen gold chain from a streetlight, lifeless and unable to hurt anyone ever again. There will be no rest for the wicked.<br /> <br /> <i>Are you ready to watch the world burn?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/508-sikker","name":"sikker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T10:23:41-08:00","id":10544,"title":"","content":"BTW, when are you finishing this book? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T10:05:13-08:00","id":15450,"title":"","content":"Wasn't there a WoD Batman fansite somewhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T20:15:26-08:00","id":15821,"title":"","content":"Was there? Can you link?<br /> I've heard of Gotham as a Durance... Batman was the Keeper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/735-hitashippo","name":"HitAShippo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T20:35:07-08:00","id":15837,"title":"","content":"It was on the old forums for a while, I was hoping someone had a link myself. Had many of the villains statted and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T13:39:06-08:00","id":20340,"title":"","content":"reminds me of the ending of the Dark Knight Returns (the comic). Are there different specializations within the Sentinels?<br /> Like Crime Scene Detectives, Streetfighters, Juggers, Assassins, Technicians ... like one for every talent the old Bat possessed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1261-doc-lumbago","name":"Doc Lumbago","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T14:56:48-08:00","id":20381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doc Lumbago</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/5262-slasher-sentinels-of-gotham?p=20340#post20340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">reminds me of the ending of the Dark Knight Returns (the comic). Are there different specializations within the Sentinels?<br /> Like Crime Scene Detectives, Streetfighters, Juggers, Assassins, Technicians ... like one for every talent the old Bat possessed?</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, probably? I figure the Undertakings of Slasher would fit the spread decently. The Sentinels recruit from all walks of life to keep their bat-utility-belt of enforcers versatile, and The Fox sponsors specialist training in a variety of fields to enhance their ability in the field, so I would definitely think most Sentinels had distinct areas of expertise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/508-sikker","name":"sikker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}